  "retainedCorrections": [
    "The initial whole-file upstream draft included unrelated unreleased parsing changes. It was never committed. This backport applies only the PR depth diff to the published npm source.",
    "The bare relative override failed ENOENT. A direct local dependency and $braces override work with both checked npm versions.",
    "The first compatibility command referenced a later initialization file absent in the release test tree. The corrected release command runs all 764 tests.",
    "The initial rebuild normalized gzip OS to 3 instead of the archive byte 255. Corrected to 255 and checked exact bytes.",
    "The initial stringify mutation was detected through expand cyclic-child processing before its named check. Reordered direct AST checks so each removed guard fails its named direct-entry assertion.",
    "The first configured deadcode run flagged direct use of a transitive test dependency. The fixture now resolves the vendored package declared dependencies generically.",
    "The first guard mutation demanded a missing exception, but a corrupt parser reached behavior checks and failed with a different error. Added independent license corruption so removal of file hashing also produces the intended missing exception.",
    "The first compatibility fault replacement matched no source text and stopped before mutation. The corrected delimiter fault fails 110 upstream tests."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The upstream proposal is open and this version is local, not a registry release. Registry audit does not validate its security.",
    "Depth checks do not bound all expansions, arbitrary malformed objects, cyclic parent pointers or every resource exhaustion path.",
    "Installed inventory covers npm package directories, not embedded bundled source. Coordinated edits to code and expected hashes still need review.",
    "Clean install checks disabled lifecycle scripts. The production build uses the owned checkout; fresh CI performs normal npm ci.",
    "Full application CI on this new source is pending. Previous exact8a14 browser/download and native evidence does not claim a new browser journey on this commit.",
    "No release, semantic quality, real participant acceptance or complete v1 claim. Crash cause remains unknown."
  ],
